1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:06,320
Many people think birds have simple minds, but ravens are a surprising exception.
许多人认为鸟类头脑简单，但渡鸦是一个令人惊讶的例外。

2
00:00:07,120 --> 00:00:11,510
Their intelligence has long been compared to that of monkeys and even humans.
长期以来，人们一直把它们的智力与猴子甚至人类的智力相提并论。

3
00:00:12,310 --> 00:00:16,500
One of the most surprising things they can do is to make plans for the future.
它们能做到的最令人惊讶的事情之一，是为未来做计划。

4
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:21,310
In one experiment, ravens were trained to use a tool to get food.
在一项实验中，渡鸦接受了训练，学习用一件工具来获取食物。

5
00:00:22,110 --> 00:00:27,850
Later, they were given a choice among several things, including the tool and some useless objects.
后来，研究人员让它们从几样东西中做出选择，其中包括那件工具和一些没用的物品。

6
00:00:28,650 --> 00:00:32,940
Most of the ravens chose the tool, even with no immediate food reward.
即使不能立刻得到食物奖励，大多数渡鸦还是选择了那件工具。

7
00:00:33,740 --> 00:00:38,410
This showed they could remember how to use the tool and plan ahead to get the treat later.
这表明，它们能记住怎样使用这件工具，还能提前计划，以便之后得到那份美食。

8
00:00:39,210 --> 00:00:41,840
Ravens are good at solving real-life problems.
渡鸦善于解决现实生活中的问题。

9
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:49,070
They use sticks to dig insects out of trees, and some even drop nuts on roads so cars can crack them open.
它们会用小树枝把昆虫从树里挖出来，有些渡鸦甚至把坚果丢在马路上，好让汽车把坚果压开。

10
00:00:49,870 --> 00:00:58,000
They can solve problems that require several steps, like using a short stick to get a longer one, then using the long stick to reach food.
它们能解决需要好几个步骤的问题，比如先用一根短树枝去取一根更长的树枝，再用这根长树枝够到食物。

11
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:01,870
Their intelligence isn’t just about solving problems.
它们的智力不仅仅体现在解决问题上。

12
00:01:02,670 --> 00:01:04,490
Ravens have rich social lives.
渡鸦的社交生活很丰富。

13
00:01:05,290 --> 00:01:09,860
They remember different faces, including those of other ravens and humans.
它们能记住不同的面孔，包括其他渡鸦和人类的面孔。

14
00:01:10,660 --> 00:01:17,000
They can hold grudges against people who have treated them badly, and even teach their young to stay away from those people.
它们会记恨那些曾经对它们不好的人，甚至会教自己的幼鸟远离这些人。

15
00:01:17,800 --> 00:01:22,190
Sadly, many kinds of ravens are suffering from habitat loss and pollution.
令人难过的是，许多种类的渡鸦正深受栖息地丧失和污染之苦。

16
00:01:22,990 --> 00:01:31,200
As we learn more about their intelligence, scientists hope people will see them as more than just “common birds” and take action to protect them.
随着我们对渡鸦的智力了解得越来越多，科学家希望人们不只把它们看作“普通的鸟”，并采取行动保护它们。
